e go together,\" she said. \"Nobody alone.\" Pike lit a fresh match and cupped it. Dell gathered Ines closer and started down, Tobin at one elbow, Mara ahead with Wen's lantern. The townsfolk pressed to the wall to let them pass, still humming, and each face they passed turned to watch. Below, the low voice faltered, then went on, as if it knew who was coming."}
